 "signs": [
  {
   "x": 8,
   "y": 2,
   "plaque": "arts_white_book",
   "theme": "arts",
   "title": "The White Book of Rhydderch",
   "text": "Llyfr Gwyn Rhydderch, the White Book of Rhydderch, was written around 1350 for a Ceredigion landowner, and it holds the earliest full texts of the Four Branches of the Mabinogi, Culhwch ac Olwen and the Welsh Arthurian romances. Its companion, the Red Book of Hergest from about 1400, is at Jesus College, Oxford. The National Library keeps the White Book here as Peniarth manuscripts 4 and 5. It is older than the printing press and the potato, and it is still read in the language it was written in."
  }
